KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Documents a CBMC bug for [expr.new]/24 on array form:
  counted *arr = new counted[3];
should call counted::counted() three times, but CBMC neither calls
the constructor nor (subsequently) the destructor under delete[].
The array-new with braced-init-list also crashes with an invariant
violation.  Discovered while writing the positive test for
[expr.new].
